.TH GREET 1 "2026-10-29" "fish lab" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
greet \- print a greeting
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B greet
[\fB\-\-name\fR \fINAME\fR]
[\fB\-\-loud\fR]
[\fB\-\-help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B greet
prints a short greeting to standard output.
It is a demonstration program written for a shell guide's lab
and does nothing else of consequence.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-name\fR \fINAME\fR
Who to greet. The default is the whole world.
.TP
.B \-\-loud
Shout the greeting in capital letters.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show a short help text and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
greet \-\-name Ada \-\-loud
